<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle on the Ice</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1242">1242</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Lake Peipus · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-crusades">Northern Crusades</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle on the Ice was fought on 5 April 1242 on frozen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-peipus">Lake Peipus</a> between the forces of the Novgorod Republic under Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-nevsky">Alexander Nevsky</a> and an army of the Livonian Order and the Bishopric of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tartu">Dorpat</a>. The crusaders were defeated, which checked their expansion into Russian lands. The battle later became a central episode of Russian national memory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-on-the-ice.jpg" alt="Battle on the Ice" width="320" height="591" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous Russian manuscript illuminators, 1560-1570s … · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Facial_Chronicle_-_b.06,_page_085_-_Battle_of_the_Ice.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
